# The claims filed as a single value, wherever in a document they sit. One row per claim whose low,
# most likely and high values coincide: a figure with no width at all.
#
# A single value is a real claim
#   "Exactly twelve people" is a stronger statement than "between ten and fourteen", and the model
#   lets somebody make it. Many claims in this corpus are single values, and almost none of them are
#   demands: a nameplate, a quantum and a window are the things somebody usually knows exactly.
#
# A single value has no range to tighten
#   So a stated `narrowsWhen` on one is either a paste from a neighbouring claim or a claim filed at
#   the wrong width. `notApplicable` is the filing that says so honestly, and it is what the schema
#   asks for here.
-- pm:Claim where low = high, at every element that carries one.
SELECT c.*
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) c
WHERE c.is_a_point
